# Audit: BLOCKED

Both critical issues (issue-1: PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED infinite loop, issue-2: resume key correlation) have been properly fixed and verified in code. The executor now uses client.COMPLETED_STATES dynamically (issue-13), and MegaUnitState persists processing_keys for Vertex line-order correlation across resume. Issue 5 (cancel_batch QUEUED) is fixed. Issue 9 (ADC error) is partially fixed — _get_client() now wraps with helpful message but _get_storage_client() still doesn't (downgraded from critical concern since genai client typically fails first). Issue 10 (JSON parse per-line) and issue 15 (download logging) are fixed. Issue 11 (model name comment) is fixed. All 28 existing batch tests pass without modification, no new regressions introduced. Remaining open warnings are: issue-3 and issue-4 (no Vertex-specific tests or factory routing tests — these are test gaps, not runtime bugs), issue-6 (bucket validation at init time — edge case), and the partial issue-9 coverage. Remaining suggestions (issues 7, 8, 12, 14) are minor edge cases and test improvements. Verdict remains FAIL due to the 2 outstanding warning-level test gaps (issue-3, issue-4) and 1 remaining edge-case warning (issue-6) — the lack of ANY Vertex-specific tests means the implementation is untested beyond code review, which is a meaningful risk for a new provider integration.

## Issues

- [critical] PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED state not handled in executor polling loop. The executor's polling loop (executor.py:744-769) only checked for SUCCEEDED, FAILED, CANCELLED, and EXPIRED. (pdf2epub/core/executor/executor.py:754)
- [critical] Line-order key correlation breaks on resume. VertexBatchClient stored submitted key orders in self._job_keys (an in-memory dict). On resume, a fresh VertexBatchClient was instantiated with empty _job_keys. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:512)
- [warning] No VertexBatchClient unit tests exist. There are zero tests for the VertexBatchClient class — no tests for client initialization, GCS bucket auto-creation, JSONL serialization (Vertex format), key correlation in get_results(), error handling for GCS failures, PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED handling, or _cleanup_gcs. The existing FakeBatchClient has no Vertex-specific capabilities. (tests/)
- [warning] No factory routing tests for Vertex provider. _create_batch_client_from_config() has Vertex-specific routing logic (factory_v2.py:407-425) but no tests verify provider=='vertex' creates VertexBatchClient, provider=='gemini' still creates GeminiBatchClient, or missing vertex config returns None. (tests/test_factories.py)
- [warning] cancel_batch --all missed QUEUED state for Vertex jobs. (pdf2epub/commands/cancel_batch.py:94)
- [warning] User-specified bucket is not validated at initialization time. When the user provides a bucket name in config, _ensure_bucket() only runs during submit(), not during __init__(). If the bucket doesn't exist or user lacks permissions, the error surfaces mid-batch-submission after prompts have been built for hundreds of units. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:496)
- [suggestion] No bucket location mismatch detection. If the user specifies a bucket in 'us-east1' but location is 'us-central1', cross-region data transfer occurs silently. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:549)
- [suggestion] GCS API not-enabled error not handled distinctly. The _ensure_bucket() handles 409 and 403 specifically, but doesn't handle the case where storage.googleapis.com API is not enabled, which falls through to generic raise. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:565)
- [warning] ADC failure does not produce a clear, actionable error message. _get_client() now wraps genai.Client with helpful messaging. However, _get_storage_client() at line 545 still creates storage.Client() without wrapping ADC errors, so if the genai client succeeds but the GCS client fails on ADC, the error is still opaque. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:545)
- [warning] JSON parse errors in GCS result files previously aborted the entire result set. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:749)
- [suggestion] Model name format difference between Gemini and Vertex not documented in code. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:643)
- [suggestion] QUEUED and CANCELLING states not classified in any 'active' states set for consistent state classification across components. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:109)
- [suggestion] Executor hardcoded batch terminal states instead of using client.COMPLETED_STATES. (pdf2epub/core/executor/executor.py:754)
- [suggestion] FakeBatchClient doesn't support Vertex-specific states (QUEUED, PARTIALLY_SUCCEEDED, CANCELLING). No existing tests exercise these states through the executor. (tests/fixtures/fake_batch.py:81)
- [suggestion] No logging of GCS download URI when retrieving results. (pdf2epub/utils/batch_utils.py:742)
